@model Student
@*
    Views/Students/Create.cshtml — PRE-TYPED, NOT TODAY'S TOPIC.

    Views are Session 18. This form is given to you finished so that the
    whole of today's lecture time goes on the CONTROLLER — which is the
    thing that actually decides what happens to what this form sends.

    Three things in here are worth a glance even though you are not
    writing them today, because Block 3 and Block 4 refer to them:

      asp-for="FullName"
          Generates <input name="FullName">. The name of the input is
          what the browser sends, and matching that name to a property is
          exactly how model binding fills the Student object in Block 2.

      asp-validation-for="FullName"
          The empty span where an error message appears IF one exists.
          Nothing writes into it unless validation failed.

      asp-validation-summary="ModelOnly"
          A list at the top for errors that belong to the whole form
          rather than to one field.

    The <form> tag with asp-action also quietly adds a hidden
    anti-forgery token. Block 3 says what that is and why the POST would
    be rejected without it.
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Add a Student";
}

<h1 class="display-5">Add a Student</h1>
<p class="lead">Everything typed here is sent to the POST version of <code>Create</code>.</p>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <form asp-action="Create" method="post">
            <div asp-validation-summary="ModelOnly" class="text-danger"></div>

            <div class="mb-3">
                <label asp-for="FullName" class="form-label">Full Name</label>
                <input asp-for="FullName" class="form-control" />
                <span asp-validation-for="FullName" class="text-danger"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-3">
                <label asp-for="YearOfStudy" class="form-label">Year of Study</label>
                <input asp-for="YearOfStudy" class="form-control" />
                <span asp-validation-for="YearOfStudy" class="text-danger"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="mb-3">
                <label asp-for="Gpa" class="form-label">GPA</label>
                <input asp-for="Gpa" class="form-control" />
                <span asp-validation-for="Gpa" class="text-danger"></span>
            </div>

            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
            <a href="/students" class="btn btn-secondary">Cancel</a>
        </form>
    </div>
</div>
